    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide011Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide011Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Self-Custody</dt><dd>Direct control of the keys needed to spend bitcoin.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Custody</dt><dd>Control over the keys or authorization needed to move bitcoin.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Wallet</dt><dd>Software or hardware that manages keys, constructs transactions, and helps users interact with Bitcoin.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Private key</dt><dd>Secret cryptographic material used to authorize spending.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Seed phrase</dt><dd>A human-readable backup representation used by many wallets to derive keys under a wallet standard.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Multisig</dt><dd>A spending condition requiring a defined threshold of multiple keys to authorize a transaction.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Cold storage</dt><dd>A custody setup intended to keep signing keys away from internet-connected systems.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Hot wallet</dt><dd>A wallet whose signing environment is connected to an online device or service.</dd></div></dl></section>
